    {
      "text": "I will make you fishers of men, Matt. 4:19 (Mark 1:17; Luke 5:10). whosoever shall do and teach them, Matt. 5:19. go rather to the lost sheep of the house of Israel, Matt. 10:6. he departed thence to teach and to preach, Matt. 11:1. gospel … shall be preached in all the world, Matt. 24:14. teach all nations, baptizing them, Matt. 28:19. preach the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins, Mark 1:4. that he might send them forth to preach, Mark 3:14. preach the gospel to every creature, Mark 16:15 (Morm. 9:22). sent them to preach the kingdom of God, Luke 9:2. seventy … sent them two and two before his face, Luke 10:1. when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren, Luke 22:32. ye are witnesses of these things, Luke 24:48 (Acts 1:8). the fields … are white already to harvest, John 4:35. go and bring forth fruit, John 15:16. Feed my sheep, John 21:17. ceased not to teach and preach Jesus, Acts 5:42. believed Philip preaching the things concerning the kingdom, Acts 8:12. commanded us to preach unto the people, Acts 10:42. Paul … reasoned with them out of the scriptures, Acts 17:2. how shall they preach, except they be sent, Rom. 10:15. we preach Christ crucified, 1 Cor. 1:23. woe is unto me, if I preach not the gospel, 1 Cor. 9:16. I declare unto you the gospel, 1 Cor. 15:1. preach not ourselves, but Christ, 2 Cor. 4:5. Preach the word; be instant in season, 2 Tim. 4:2. another angel … having the everlasting gospel to preach, Rev. 14:6.",
